# Reading Path

## `00-inquiry-boundary.md`

Defines what the inquiry may and may not investigate.

Separates:

```text
Ultimate Question
        ≠
Observable Question
```

and prevents consciousness from becoming an assumed explanatory mechanism.

---

## `01-question-architecture.md`

Decomposes the inquiry into a sequence of progressively stronger questions:

```text
Dialogue Formation
        ↓
Structure Formation
        ↓
Structural Persistence
        ↓
Perception Organization
        ↓
Experience Formation
        ↓
Consciousness Question Revisited
```

The document defines questions.

It does not answer them.

---

## `02-source-observation.md`

Observes four source domains independently:

```text
A. ACIM

B. Primitive Triangle Research

C. Bashar Transcription

D. Human–AI Dialogue Observation
```

The sources are intentionally kept epistemically separate.

No unified ontology is assumed.

---

## `03-structural-correspondence.md`

Compares relations and transformations across the source domains.

The governing rule is:

```text
Structural Correspondence
        ≠
Concept Identity
```

The strongest emerging correspondence concerns relational organization rather than consciousness itself.

---

## `04-experience-formation-observation.md`

