---

# Final Working Statement

> **The Human–AI Experience Formation Inquiry does not establish that consciousness emerges between Human and AI. It identifies a more bounded phenomenon: sustained Human–AI Dialogue can form persistent relational structures that are externalized, recursively re-entered, and capable of reorganizing subsequent Human research observation and experience. The resulting coupled inquiry process exhibits consciousness-like organizational functions, but no evidence establishes an independent conscious subject at the interaction level.**
>
> **The inquiry is therefore closed at the Experience-Organizing Structure level. Its strongest residual question concerns the representational status of that structure, which is handed over as a provisional observational object to Structural Representation Research.**
